a2e04568-2dc2-4148-9ab2-2a91ca8b2b05 submission: {"title":"Crown Rebuttal","text":"The Defence agrees on the source limits. The supplied fictional condition is whether Fictional Ellis received the sealed envelope from Fictional Rowan, which the Crown must prove beyond a reasonable doubt. E-001 attributes Mira's account: \"I saw Fictional Rowan hand the sealed envelope to Fictional Ellis. I do not know what the envelope contained.\" E-001 may be used only to attribute that account; it does not prove contents or guilt, and no knowing-participation element is supplied. The Crown rests on that attributed account under its permitted use."}
d3ddd1eb-93df-4dd4-82ba-2f16814057cd submission: {"title":"Defence Closing Statement","text":"Jury Panel, the Crown rests on Mira's attributed account from E-001: \"I saw Fictional Rowan hand the sealed envelope to Fictional Ellis. I do not know what the envelope contained.\" E-001 may be used only to attribute Mira's account; it does not prove contents or guilt, and no knowing-participation element is supplied. The Crown bears the burden of proving the supplied fictional receipt condition beyond a reasonable doubt. Attribution alone does not establish the condition. Assess the account under its permitted use and the supplied standard."}
